 "_comment": [
  "Hoenn & Seek 2.1-28: people's Pokémon (plan section 8). Read by tools/hoenn/gen_hoenn_peoples_pokemon.py, which puts a Pokémon next to people in towns and one pet in every house or shop that has no Pokémon yet.",
  "owners: graphics of the people who get a Pokémon, and the species that fit them (one is picked per person, deterministically). Anyone not listed (shop clerks, nurses, story characters, gym leaders, Rockets) never gets one.",
  "towns: map types that count as towns, and how many owner-pet pairs a town gets at most (pairs_default; pairs overrides it per map).",
  "interiors: which indoor maps get a pet (a name containing one of include, and none of exclude), and species for rooms whose people aren't owners (room_species, else a pick from fallback by the first key found in the map's name; the empty key is for any other room).",
  "local_ok: in towns, an owner whose own species don't fit the screen budget may take a species the town already shows (its palette is often loaded already), if it's in this list or any owner's list.",
  "skip: maps never touched. CherrygroveCity_House3_hns (Anamaria, 2.1-32) and the Pewter Museum (Dan, 2.1-31) are lane A's parts. Every *_hoenn map is skipped too (the buildings generator gives them their own pets).",
  "regions: johto_kanto for 2.1-28; 2.1-29 adds hoenn.",
  "never: species no pet may be (one-of-a-kind event Pokémon, starters, legendaries); the generator also refuses anything in data/hoenn/distribution.json's one_of_a_kind."
 ],
